<!--
  Keep every live DK draft queue stocked, every 5 minutes.

      cp tools/com.bba.autoqueue.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bba.autoqueue.plist
      launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.bba.autoqueue.plist   # stop it

  This one WRITES to your DraftKings entries — it is the only job here that does. It
  sets the draft queue, which is what DK drafts from when a pick clock expires, so
  while it is loaded it is deciding your picks in your absence. Two guards on that:

    --deadline  is a wall-clock stop. Past it every run exits without touching a
                queue, so a timer left loaded goes quiet instead of drafting your
                board overnight. Edit the date below to extend it; there is no way
                to extend it by accident.

    the tool    never discards a player you queued by hand — yours stay, in front,
                and the recommender fills in behind. The --replace flag overrides
                that, and is deliberately not used here.

  Five minutes against a ten-minute pick clock: the queue is never more than one pick
  behind the board. Most runs write nothing and say "queue already correct".

  --max-until-clock 2 keeps each pass to the boards near your pick. It is free to
  apply: picksUntilOnTheClock arrives in the one live-drafts call, so a skipped draft
  costs no 700KB draftStatus. It is safe because every board is already queued and DK
  removes drafted players from a queue itself — a queue left alone gets shorter, never
  wrong — and --sweep-minutes 30 refreshes anything that has gone untouched anyway.

  StartInterval, not StartCalendarInterval: this wants "every so often", and launchd
  fires once shortly after a wake rather than replaying every missed run.

  NOTE the paths below point at the worktree the fix was built in, because that is
  where tools/auto-queue.py currently lives. Merge to master and repoint them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.bba.autoqueue</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/jvonderhoff/Development/projects/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/.venv/bin/python</string>
        <string>/Users/jvonderhoff/Development/projects/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/.claude/worktrees/beautiful-rhodes-84e22b/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/tools/auto-queue.py</string>
        <string>--depth</string>
        <string>6</string>
        <string>--max-until-clock</string>
        <string>2</string>
        <string>--deadline</string>
        <string>2026-09-07T21:00</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/jvonderhoff/Development/projects/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/.claude/worktrees/beautiful-rhodes-84e22b/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft</string>

    <!-- every 5 minutes -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jvonderhoff/Development/projects/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/data/autoqueue/autoqueue.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/jvonderhoff/Development/projects/fantasy_football/best-ball-draft/data/autoqueue/autoqueue.err</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
